# The build context is the repo root. docker/, scripts/, patches/ and vllm/ are
# what the build graph actually reads from it -- vllm/ since the vllm bake
# target started building the vendored fork (docker/vllm.Dockerfile). The rest
# is documentation, host-side tooling, investigation output (the ORT
# backend-test logs run to tens of megabytes), and the archived rocm7.14/ and
# rocm6.4.4/ lines.
#
# This does not affect layer caching. BuildKit keys a COPY or a bind mount on the
# checksums of the files it actually reads, not on the whole context.
*.md
*.log
tools/
rocm7.14/
rocm6.4.4/
llama-cpp-gfx803/

# The bare "*.md" rule above matches only the context root -- BuildKit's
# ignore patterns are not gitignore's recursive globs, so it drops the root
# AGENTS.md and README.md but not a nested one, and needs its own line here for
# vllm/AGENTS.md (upstream's own PR policy; see this repo's AGENTS.md, "vLLM
# lives in vllm/ as a hard fork" for why it does not apply), vllm/BUILD.md and
# vllm/NOTES.md. docs/, tests/, examples/, benchmarks/ and .buildkite/ are the
# fork's own bulk that the build never reads; build/ and *.egg-info/ are local
# artifacts a host build can leave behind.
vllm/*.md
vllm/docs/
vllm/tests/
vllm/examples/
vllm/benchmarks/
vllm/.buildkite/
vllm/build/
vllm/*.egg-info/
